+### Feature A/B matrix: which model measures which knob
+
+The matrix above measures the engine's baseline thesis (streaming vs mmap). The engine also ships
+a compute/latency-hiding layer that the per-model cells do not touch: speculative decode
+(`--mtp`, `--ngram`), cache-aware routing (`--expert-substitute`, `--drop-cold-experts`,
+`--drop-in-prefill`, `--route-ahead`), I/O timing (`--io-two-wave`, `--prefetch`), and the
+serve/load variants (`--row-stream`, `--dense-odirect`, `--release-mmap`). Each gets its A/B on
+the model that isolates its mechanism with the least confound; where two models give the same
+insight, the faster one runs first. All of these are our own implementations except the ngram
+draft source (mainline `ngram-cache`, consumed by our verify loop).
+
+| Priority | Model (profile) | Feature A/B | Insight sought |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | OLMoE (fastest, fits RAM) | `--ngram` (standard + code-repetition prompt) | pure speculation gain, zero thrash confound; ngram feeds on prompt repetition, so the edit/code workload is its habitat |
+| 2 | OLMoE | `--dense-odirect`, `--ubatch` | cheapest runs; dense reads are its only remaining I/O, so the delta is unambiguous; fills the ubatch-512 protocol-justification row |
+| 3 | LFM2.5 (hybrid, fits RAM) | `--ngram` | does speculative verify compose with recurrent-state rollback planes? |
+| 4 | Ling-mini (marginal fits-RAM) | `--row-stream` | can serve-time dense row streaming shrink the resident sum and recover the −31 % penalty? |
+| 5 | Cyber-Tiel (MTP carrier) | `--mtp` | the only model with MTP heads; the only multiplicative lever we've built; A/B vs its cell (b), quality column alongside per the lossy rule |
+| 6 | Cyber-Tiel (highest miss headroom) | `--expert-substitute`, `--drop-cold-experts`, `--drop-in-prefill`, `--route-ahead` | ~18 % cache misses to win back on the worst-case model; report `experts_substituted`/`experts_dropped`/`experts_routed` with the tok/s |
+| 7 | Qwen3.6 (deepest thrash) | `--io-two-wave`, `--prefetch` | maximum stall signal (533 majflt/tok); short runs — the metrics are majflt/stall, not answer length; `--release-mmap` load-peak metric rides along |
+| 8 | Cyber-Tiel | `--predict-prefetch` (+`--predict-spec-max`) | composition test: prefetch driven by speculated tokens; only after the MTP row exists |
+
+Cyber-Tiel rows 5/6/8 share one load session (load is the expensive part at 21 GB). Lossy knobs
+report their quality evidence in the same row — that is the rule, not a preference.
